      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To simplify the expression \\((x^5 + x^4 + x + 10) - (x^5 + 2x^4 - x^3 + 12)\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses.\n2. Combine like terms.\n\nLet's start with the given expression:\n\\[\n(x^5 + x^4 + x + 10) - (x^5 + 2x^4 - x^3 + 12)\n\\]\n\nDistribute the negative sign:\n\\[\nx^5 + x^4 + x + 10 - x^5 - 2x^4 + x^3 - 12\n\\]\n\nNow, combine the like terms:\n\\[\n(x^5 - x^5) + (x^4 - 2x^4) + x^3 + x + (10 - 12)\n\\]\n\nSimplify each group of like terms:\n\\[\n0 + (-x^4) + x^3 + x + (-2)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n-x^4 + x^3 + x - 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified polynomial is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-x^4 + x^3 + x - 2}\n\\]",
